[91.830289, "i", "cat > /home/user/BUGFIX_SUMMARY.txt << 'EOF'\nSURICATA CORRELATION SCRIPT - BUG FIX SUMMARY\n==============================================\n\nPROBLEM:\nThe correlation script was finding 80% fewer lateral movement candidates\ncompared to the old Zeek-based pipeline.\n\nROOT CAUSE:\nTwo bugs in /home/user/correlate.py:\n\n1. CRITICAL BUG - Wrong event_type:\n   - Script checked for event_type == \"netflow\"\n   - Suricata actually uses event_type == \"flow\"\n   - Result: Script processed ZERO flow events\n\n2. SECONDARY BUG - Wrong timestamp format:\n   - Script used: \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"\n   - Suricata uses: \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%f%z\" (with microseconds and timezone)\n   - Result: Would have caused parsing errors once bug #1 was fixed\n\nFIXES APPLIED:\n- Changed event_type check from \"netflow\" to \"flow\"\n- Updated timestamp parsing to handle microseconds and timezone\n- Backup saved to /home/user/correlate.py.backup\n\nRESULTS:\n- Script now successfully processes internal-to-internal flow events\n- Detected lateral movement candidate: 10.1"]
[91.830439, "i", ".5.23\n- Host 10.1.5.23 connected to 12+ distinct internal hosts within 5 minutes\n- Detection pattern matches expected scanning behavior\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- Confirmed eve.json contains \"flow\" events (not \"netflow\")\n- Confirmed internal-to-internal traffic exists in logs\n- Confirmed timestamp format: 2024-01-10T00:00:13.316061+0000\n- Script now correctly identifies scanning activity\nEOF\n"]
